 "path": "memory/continual-arc-panel-intersection.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC: paired-panel intersection rule\n\nA demonstrated task family presents two same-height binary-pattern panels separated by a solid-color vertical divider. Produce a grid the width of one panel (drop the divider and right panel): output color 2 exactly where corresponding cells in the left panel are nonzero AND cells in the right panel are nonzero; otherwise output 0. Preserve row/column alignment. In the demo, left color 3 and right color 8 intersected to form 2s; in the solved instance, left color 5 and right color 6 intersected to form 2s. The divider color/width and foreground colors can vary. Verify output shape from panel widths and check overlap row by row.\n"
}
